  "holistic_F_N": 0,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all thermal incidents within 24 hours and customer notice within 72 hours. S2 keeps a 55 °C test and 5% corrective-action threshold, with per-model results given to customers but only aggregated public disclosure. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 12 months and retrofit at 6 years with a feasibility escape; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 uses an 8/100k investigation trigger without automatic recall, with notices without delay."
